draft_notes.limitations:
The program assumes the constructor's domain:
- slots are square glyphs of side h, at a regular pitch of h+1 along the band axis;
- consecutive bands are separated by at least one blank line;
- every glyph touches both ends of the band, which the generator guarantees by requiring rows 0 and 2 to be used;
- the background is palette[0].

If the outermost band does not span the full glyph thickness, the inferred h would be wrong. The generator never produces this.

The fixtures match the uniform rule, and I found no constructor defects; I have not run the factory or emitted program. The colour tie-break (smallest value) is only a deterministic fallback; each slot is single-coloured in-domain.
